.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-LIST-OBJECT-VERSIONS 1 "November 2026" "euclid-cli 2.1.3" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-list-object-versions \- list every version of an object
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm list-object-versions
.BR \-\-bucket | \-b
.I NAME|ERN
.BR \-\-key | \-k
.I KEY
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists every version of one object: the current one first, marked
.BR "\(dqlatest\(dq: true" ,
then the non-current versions a bucket with versioning has kept, the most
recently replaced first. See
.BR euclid-cli-esm-set-bucket-versioning (1).
.PP
Each version carries its
.IR versionId ,
.IR size ,
.IR md5Sum ,
.IR contentType ,
.IR status ,
.I lifecycleState
and when it was stored
.RI ( modified ).
An object stored before versioning was turned on has an empty
.I versionId
until it is replaced, when it is given one.
.PP
In a bucket without versioning, the list is the current object alone.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket " " \fINAME|ERN\fR
The object's bucket, by name or ERN. Required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
The object's key within the bucket. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The versions are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing or invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, the
caller may not read the bucket, or the key has no object and no versions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli esm list-object-versions --bucket incoming --key feed.xml

# download the version before the current one
euclid-cli esm download-file --bucket incoming --key feed.xml --file feed-previous.xml \e
    --version-id "$(euclid-cli esm list-object-versions --bucket incoming --key feed.xml \e
                    | jq -r '.versions[1].versionId')"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-set-bucket-versioning (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-download-file (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-delete-object (1)
